# Local development environment. Copy to `.env`; npm start and npm run dev load it.
# Production deployments set real environment variables instead.

# --- Site key ---------------------------------------------------------------
# This key protects saved credentials and derives signing secrets. Local sites create their
# own key automatically outside the portable site directory; no Generate click is needed.
# To supply the key through the environment, use a hex value of at least 32 bytes.
# TOVU_SITE_KEY is the only environment name read for the site key.
# Back up the existing key privately. Without it, saved credentials cannot be recovered.
# `docker compose up` (docker-compose.yml) refuses to start while this is unset or empty.
TOVU_SITE_KEY=

# --- Optional ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Seeded admin credentials. Default to admin / tovu-dev when unset (identity/wiring.ts).
# Optional for local development only — under TOVU_RUNTIME_MODE=production the boot gate REFUSES
# to start while TOVU_ADMIN_PASSWORD is unset or still the default (PRODUCTION_BOOT_UNSAFE_DEFAULT).
# Seeded on first boot only, stored as an argon2id hash; changing it later does nothing to an
# existing install — use Users → Reset password in the admin.
# TOVU_ADMIN_USER=admin
# TOVU_ADMIN_PASSWORD=tovu-dev

# Ports. dev.mjs preflights each one and names the process holding it rather than failing obscurely.
# PORT=3000
# TOVU_ADMIN_DEV_PORT=5173
# JINI_AGENT_DAEMON_PORT=4319

# Which proxies to trust for the client IP in X-Forwarded-For (per-IP rate limits, stored form
# source IPs). Unset: none locally; on Fly (FLY_APP_NAME set) exactly one hop, Fly's edge. Set it
# when Tovu runs behind another reverse proxy: the number of proxy hops in front of it (e.g. 1),
# or a list of proxy addresses/subnets (e.g. "loopback, 10.0.0.0/8"). "false" or 0 trusts none.
# "true" is refused at boot: it would let any client spoof its IP.
# TOVU_TRUST_PROXY=1

# Legacy gap-discovery diagnostic: also disables local-owner native fallbacks and selects
# the strict prohibition prompt. Prefer TOVU_AGENT_NATIVE_FALLBACKS=0 to restore the normal lock.
# This is a tool-availability switch, not an OS filesystem security boundary.
# TOVU_AGENT_FORBID_BASH=1

# Tracing (OpenTelemetry). Off unless an OTLP endpoint is set; then Tovu exports spans for
# inbound requests, database queries, outbound HTTP calls and admin-chat agent runs over OTLP/HTTP.
# Standard OpenTelemetry names, so Datadog (Agent OTLP receiver) and Grafana (Alloy/Tempo/Cloud
# OTLP gateway) need no Tovu-specific setup. How-to: development/docs/deployment/observability.md.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318        # base URL; /v1/traces is appended
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT=                      # full traces URL; wins over the base
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=Authorization=Basic%20xxxx    # collector auth (Grafana Cloud, etc.)
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=tovu

# --- Docker (docker-compose.yml) ---------------------------------------------
#
# `docker compose` reads `.env` from this directory too, by its own mechanism — unrelated to
# dev.mjs's loader above, and unaffected by the note at the top that `npm start` ignores `.env`.
# The same file therefore serves both a local `npm run dev` and a container run.

# THE SWITCH THAT ARMS EVERY PRODUCTION SAFETY CHECK, and the only signal consulted for it —
# NODE_ENV is never read for this purpose (src/core/runtime-mode.ts). Anything other than the
# literal "production" resolves to `local`, which activates NO containment: no boot gate, no
# default-password refusal, no capability containment. Leave it unset for local development.
# TOVU_RUNTIME_MODE=production

# Local owner chats may fall back to native Bash/file edits after trying Tovu tools.
# Every fallback is recorded in Observability > Tool gaps. Set 0 to disable again.
# Visitors/non-owners and production/hosted deployments never receive this grant.
# TOVU_AGENT_NATIVE_FALLBACKS=0

# Host port the container publishes on. The container always listens on 3000 internally.
# TOVU_PORT=3000

# BUILD-time, not runtime: installs headless Chromium into the image for browser-backed tools
# (site_collect_page_evidence, web_screenshot_page). Off by default (owner decision 2026-10-08) —
# it adds ~150MB+ to the image and ~150–250 MB of RAM per capture. Rebuild after changing it.
# TOVU_INSTALL_BROWSER=1
